# Example 1614: Repeated insertion into the same ordinal gap
# Regression test: inserting before the minimum many times along one path
# must keep working. Ordinal values are allocated by midpoint, so each
# insertion halves the gap below the minimum. The model checker respaces
# the stored ordinal IDs by rank before the gap runs out.
# Demonstrates: segments(before=...), ordinal ID respacing

# Only one timestamp is live at a time, so the limit never binds. Every
# state is distinct (count differs), so symmetry reduction cannot merge
# the path: all 100 insertions run back to back into the head gap.

TIMES = symmetry.ordinal(name="ts", limit=2)

action Init:
    t = TIMES.fresh()
    count = 0

atomic fair action InsertBefore:
    require count < 100
    gap = oneof TIMES.segments(before=t)
    t = gap.fresh()
    count += 1

always eventually assertion ReachesHundred:
    return count == 100
